{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/testing/architecture/runtime-entity-names","title":"Unique runtime entity names","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"unique-runtime-entity-names","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Unique runtime entity names"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"function","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"keepRuntimeEntityNamesUnique","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"graph"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"ArchitectureGraph","kind":"type"},{"text":") {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"assertRuntimeEntityNamesUnique","kind":"function"},{"text":"(graph.graph);","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"}","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"assertRuntimeEntityNamesUnique"},{"t":"text","text":" requires every Craft service and every"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"primitive to have a distinct name across the application graph. The check"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"compares the names as written, across kinds: a "},{"t":"code","text":"query"},{"t":"text","text":", a "},{"t":"code","text":"state"},{"t":"text","text":", an"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"asyncProcess"},{"t":"text","text":", and a "},{"t":"code","text":"craftService"},{"t":"text","text":" cannot reuse the same name."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"before-two-entities-named-user","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Before: two entities named "},{"t":"code","text":"User"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"user"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"query","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'User'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  loader: loadUser,","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"selectedUser"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"state","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'User'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  initialValue: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"null","kind":"keyword"},{"text":",","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"typescript","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This fails even though the entities have different primitive kinds. A replay"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"or restore mechanism needs a stable way to address one runtime entity without"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"guessing whether "},{"t":"code","text":"User"},{"t":"text","text":" means the query or the state."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"after-give-each-entity-its-own-name","children":[{"t":"text","text":"After: give each entity its own name"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"user"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"query","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'currentUserQuery'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  loader: loadUser,","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[]},{"tokens":[{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"selectedUser"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"yield*","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"state","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'selectedUserState'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  initialValue: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"null","kind":"keyword"},{"text":",","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"typescript","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Use distinct descriptive names for services and all primitives. The rule"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"reports the duplicated name and each source location; choose and apply the new"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"names manually because only the application author knows which identity other"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"systems may already rely on. There is no automatic fix."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"why-names-are-project-wide","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Why names are project-wide"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Replay, snapshots, breakpoints, and dependency overrides can use the name as a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"stable handle for a runtime entity. That makes it possible for a restore setup"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"to select a specific service or primitive and substitute a dependency before"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"resuming. For example, a replay can replace the dependency that supplies a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"user's permissions so a product-manager flow can be resumed consistently,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"even if the currently connected user would otherwise receive admin"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"permissions. The unique name identifies the entity to override; the replay and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dependency override mechanisms perform the restoration and substitution."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The declarative architecture baseline runs this check for the whole graph:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"assertDeclarativeArchitecture","kind":"function"},{"text":"(graph.graph);","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"typescript","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"See "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/testing/architecture/declarative-baseline","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"the architecture baseline"}]},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"and the "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/testing/architecture#built-in-helpers","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"built-in helper list"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"before-two-entities-named-user","text":"Before: two entities named User"},{"level":2,"id":"after-give-each-entity-its-own-name","text":"After: give each entity its own name"},{"level":2,"id":"why-names-are-project-wide","text":"Why names are project-wide"}]}